## Design notes

- **`favorite` as `@api` getter/setter over a private `_favorite` field** — the parent can push a new value at any time (server refresh), and the button re-renders because `_favorite` is reactive. The public API is never reassigned directly.
- **Optimistic UI** — the click handler flips `_favorite` first, then dispatches `favoritechange` with `detail: { favorite: <new value> }`.
- **Accessibility** — one native `<button type="button">`, `aria-pressed` as the string `"true"`/`"false"`, and `aria-label`/`title` both bound to the label of the action the click will perform (Remove when favourited, Add when not). The `lightning-icon` is purely decorative since the button carries the accessible name.
- **i18n** — both labels come from `@salesforce/label/c.*`; no hard-coded text. The icon variant (`warning` vs `bare`) gives the icon-style visual state without extra text.

